---
interface Props {
  product: {
    name: string;
    publisher: string;
    system: string;
    price: number;
    currency: string;
    levels?: {
      min: number;
      max: number;
    };
    affiliateLink?: string;
  };
  class?: string;
}

const { product, class: className } = Astro.props;
---

<div class:list={["bg-white p-6 rounded-2xl border border-copper-200 shadow-sm", className]}>
  <h3 class="font-serif font-bold text-xl mb-6 text-copper-900 border-b border-copper-100 pb-2">Product Details</h3>
  <ul class="space-y-4 text-sm text-copper-700">
    <li class="flex justify-between">
      <span class="text-copper-500">Publisher</span>
      <span class="font-medium text-right">{product.publisher}</span>
    </li>
    <li class="flex justify-between">
      <span class="text-copper-500">System</span>
      <span class="font-medium text-right">{product.system}</span>
    </li>
     <li class="flex justify-between">
      <span class="text-copper-500">Price</span>
      <span class="font-medium text-right text-green-700 font-bold">{product.currency === 'USD' ? '$' : product.currency}{product.price}</span>
    </li>
    {product.levels && (
         <li class="flex justify-between">
          <span class="text-copper-500">Levels</span>
          <span class="font-medium text-right">{product.levels.min}-{product.levels.max}</span>
        </li>
    )}
  </ul>
  
  {/* Desktop CTA Button (Hidden if handled externally, or we can keep it here) 
      The requirement says: "make a CTA bar bellow the box for the pc view".
      If we include it here, it will appear wherever this component is used.
      Mobile needs a sticky bar, so we might want to conditionally hide this on mobile 
      or just use this component for the box content and handle CTA separately?
      
      User said: "CTA bar bellow the box for the pc view ... In the phone view you need to also add the bar in the bottom"
      
      Let's include the button here, but we might hide it on certain breakpoints if the sticky bar covers it?
      Actually, the sticky bar is for phone. This button is for PC.
      If we use this component on phone (in the content flow), the button will appear there too.
      That might be redundant with the sticky bar.
      Let's render it here, and maybe hide it on mobile via CSS class if needed.
  */}
  {product.affiliateLink && (
    <a href={product.affiliateLink} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="hidden md:block mt-8 w-full bg-tradewind-600 hover:bg-tradewind-500 text-white text-center font-bold py-4 rounded-xl transition-all shadow-md hover:shadow-lg transform hover:-translate-y-0.5">
      Check the book in Amazon
    </a>
  )}
</div>
